It calls the official APIs of RTE (Réseau de transport d'électricité) on the
RTE data portal (https://data.rte-france.com), "Signal" 2.0 and "Demand
Response Signal" 2.0, with the client id and client secret of the user's own
application, and the user accepts the terms of use of the RTE data portal.
RTE is a trademark of RTE Réseau de transport d'électricité; this integration
is not affiliated with nor endorsed by RTE.

Sources
-------
The endpoints, parameters, answers and error codes come from the user guides
of both APIs published by RTE (Signal 2.0, Demand Response Signal 2.0.01).
The PP day rules (22 days from 1 November to 31 March, working days without
public holidays, peak periods 7:00-10:00 and 17:00-20:00) come from the
deliberation 2026-24 of the French energy regulator (CRE) of 27 January 2026.
The idea of the integration comes from the Home Assistant custom component
"rte-jours-signales" by hiteule (Apache-2.0); no code was copied from it.
